  verifiable-gemma applies the CommitLLM commit-and-audit protocol to Gemma 4. The protocol design
  and its vocabulary follow CommitLLM: commit / audit / opening, routine and full audit tiers,
  Freivalds checks per matrix family, bridge replay, captured-logits decode with LM-head binding,
  receipt bindings (prompt, manifest, seed, token count, IO chain), reason-code style, and the
  verified / audited / open claim boundary with its residual hole (the consistent fake attention
  output, as described in the CommitLLM README). The adversarial suite (tests/test_adversarial_tiny.py)
  mirrors the scenario list of scripts/modal/tests/llama/test_adversarial.py.

  Files read for structure only; no code was copied or adapted:
    README.md, LICENSE, scripts/modal/tests/llama/test_adversarial.py (scenario names and expected
    rejection classes)

  If code is copied from CommitLLM in the future, keep its MIT header and add a line here:
    <upstream path> -> <local path>: <what changed>

Model: Gemma 4 by Google DeepMind
  google/gemma-4-12B-it and google/gemma-4-31B-it, Apache License 2.0.
  No weights are distributed with this repository. The tiny test checkpoint is randomly
  initialised from a shrunk copy of the Gemma 4 12B text configuration.

Reference implementation: Hugging Face transformers (Apache License 2.0)
  src/transformers/models/gemma4/modeling_gemma4.py, models/gemma4_unified/modeling_gemma4_unified.py
  and modeling_rope_utils.py (proportional RoPE) were read to write the canonical functions in
  src/vgemma/canon.py, which are tested against those modules; no code was copied.
